# landhorse replaces Seahorse: it installs the seahorse command, a hidden
# org.gnome.seahorse.Application desktop entry and Seahorse's GSettings schema, so the
# packages that depend on seahorse (desktop metapackages, libreoffice-gnome,
# openpgp-applet and others; gnome needs seahorse >= 3.36) keep working.
Provides: seahorse (= 47.0),
Conflicts: seahorse,
Replaces: seahorse,
Description: manage passwords, keyrings, PGP and SSH keys
 Landhorse is a replacement for GNOME's Passwords and Keys (Seahorse) with a
 conventional desktop layout: a menu bar and labelled toolbar over three panes,
 showing the type of thing, a sortable list of that type, and the details of
 the selected item.
 .
 It shows the passwords in your keyrings through the Secret Service (such as
 gnome-keyring), your GnuPG keys grouped by private or public key and by email
 address, and your OpenSSH keys. Keys can be imported, exported, published to
 keyservers and revoked.
 .
 This package replaces seahorse, and provides the seahorse command for programs
 that run it.
